<section class="faq-section" style="padding: 100px 0; background-color: var(--color-cream-bg);">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header" data-aos="fade-up">
      <h2 class="h2">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-list">
      <!-- Q1 -->
      <div class="faq-item" data-aos="fade-up">
        <button class="faq-question">
          Why is your Ghee so expensive?
          <span class="faq-icon"></span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <p>Because it is real. 30 Litres of A2 milk makes just 1 Litre of our Ghee. We pay our farmers a premium to ensure the cows are forest-grazed, and the Bilona method takes 10x more time than industrial processing. You aren't paying for butter oil; you are paying for medicine.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Q2 -->
      <div class="faq-item" data-aos="fade-up">
        <button class="faq-question">
          What do "Forest Fed" cows eat?
          <span class="faq-icon"></span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <p>They graze freely in the forest on Amruthaballi, Ashwagandha, and over 40 varieties of natural herbs and grasses. This medicinal diet is what makes the Ghee 'Vedic' and high in CLA and Omega-3s.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Q3 -->
      <div class="faq-item" data-aos="fade-up">
        <button class="faq-question">
          Is this made from Cream or Curd (Bilona)?
          <span class="faq-icon"></span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <p>Strictly Curd. Milk → Curd → Hand Churning → Butter → Ghee. Most commercial ghee uses a 'cream separator' which skips the fermentation stage. Fermentation is essential to remove lactose and create the beneficial microbes found in authentic Ghee.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Q4 -->
      <div class="faq-item" data-aos="fade-up">
        <button class="faq-question">
          Can I use this for Ayurveda?
          <span class="faq-icon"></span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <p>Yes. Our Red Cow Ghee is highly recommended for Nasya (nasal drops), Netra Basti (eye treatment), and as a carrier for Ayurvedic herbs. It is 100% pure and contains no additives.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

